{
  "about": "A reason for the first raid (the user's request; decisions DH-130 to DH-159; Book 4 section 08, 'Needs before aims'; Book 6 sections 02 and 18; Book 8 sections 05, 07, 08 and 09). The household lacks iron, grain, cloth and salt from day 1 and says so, occasionally, in its own voices and tied to what it is doing; the morning report counts the grain down and notes what ran low; on a clear day at the Hag's Seat someone points out smoke and fields on the Irish coast; the wreck-scavengers are Carrick folk who came over by skin boat to strip the wreck, as anyone would, and their boat (the skiff in Seal Cave) holds Carrick grain, nails and a net; asked, a scavenger names Carrick, and Thorkel's chart, which Oddi keeps and reads, says the same; before the launch the household sits in council at the fire, and the steerer chooses its intent, which everyone remembers. The Carrick section is Stages 15 and 16's data. Every number is Book 10's (section 22, 'Reasons for the first raid').",
